words in -ness that are better than existent forms in -ty are rare; perhaps *acuteness* & *conspicuousness* have the advantage of *acuity* & *conspicuity*; & if *perspicuousness* could be established in place of *perspicuity* it might help to obviate the common confusion with *perspicacity*;
>>>

